The disconnect window is wall-clock, but pings don't go out once per interval: `LastPingUtc` is stamped just after the tick that triggered the ping, so the `> _pingInterval` guard fails on the next tick and the ping slips a full interval. The effective period is ~2 intervals, so `3` tolerates two misses, not three — measured at both 500 ms and 10 s. A peer that pongs slower than the 3 s `Timeouts.P2PPing` gets dropped.
